Are you picturing a blockchain that starts in the middle of history, with Severodonetsk as the example?

A ledger has a first block, but a city already has generations of history on the day you start recording it. And a record about an earlier event has two dates that matter. There’s when the event supposedly happened, and when somebody put their account on the ledger. The chain can preserve the second date and the account as it was entered. The first date and the account’s accuracy still depend on the evidence.

That’s a good premise for an AI-nime. Three people remember the same street differently. All three testimonies are preserved. Years later, somebody mistakes the first one entered for the original version of what happened.